sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch16-01> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Unlike explanations of colouration as cryptic, warning or mimetic, which cannot be demonstrated, the fitness of organic form for mechanical functions such as swimming or flight can be analysed and established in detail by statics and dynamics.";
    dc:type "conceptual";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Mechanical adaptations of form are demonstrable, unlike colour adaptations";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "D’Arcy Wentworth Thompson, On Growth and Form (1st ed., Cambridge: Cambridge University Press, 1917), Chapter XVI, “On Form and Mechanical Efficiency”; topic “Mechanical fitness versus speculative adaptation”. Scope: adaptive form and colouration of animals in general"
}
